# Phase 57 Implementation Plan - Support Other Language Book Names in Title Headers

Context:
Supporting other language Book names in title headers (for Telugu, Hindi, etc.). This plan outlines the technical design for importing book name translations, storing them per Bible version in Isar database, and displaying the alias book names in the Bible Search pane, Preview pane, Slides pane, and Live Projection (Monitor 1 & Monitor 2) without altering core search logic or setlist display names.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Schema Update**: `BibleVersion` Isar model will be updated with an optional field `bookNameMappingsJson` to persist JSON-encoded book name alias mappings (`Map<String, String>`).
> 
> **Setlist Persistence Encoding**: `SavedSetlist` repository serialization format for `scripture:` items will be extended to encode `bookAlias` and `secondaryBookAlias` so that saved setlists retain imported book alias names when reloaded.

---

## Open Questions & Assumptions

> [!NOTE]
> 1. **Normalization & Conflict Handling**: Input lines in the "Import Book Names" popup will be parsed line by line. The left side (English/input book name) will be passed through `BibleConstants.normalizeBookName(...)` to convert inputs like `psalm`, `psalms`, `gen`, or `1jn` into standard canonical keys (`Psalms`, `Genesis`, `1 John`).
> 
> 2. **Setlist Display vs Slide Display**:
>    - **Setlist Pane**: Displays actual canonical book name (e.g. `Genesis 1:1-5 KJV`).
>    - **Slides Pane Title Column**: Displays alias book name (e.g. `ఆదికాండము 1:1-5 KJV`).
>    - **Preview Pane Header in Bible Search**: Displays `Genesis (ఆదికాండము) 1:1-5`.
>    - **Live Projection Headers (Monitor 1 & 2)**: Displays alias book name (e.g. `ఆదికాండము 1:1-5 KJV`).

